Sval: the macOS updater, its privileged helpers and the crash reporter are Sval's own

Mozilla's names make these Firefox's on macOS. A privileged helper's label is
its file in Contents/Library/LaunchServices, its job in launchd, and its files
under /Library/PrivilegedHelperTools and /Library/LaunchDaemons, one per label
for the whole machine. An installed Firefox's helper of the same label would
be replaced by Sval's when either is blessed (SMJobBless), and removed for both
when either update finishes. The updater's NSConnection name is one per
machine too. macOS also keeps privacy decisions (Local Network, TCC) by signing
identifier, which a helper bundle takes from its CFBundleIdentifier, so
updater.app and crashreporter.app shared Firefox's.

The updater's helper is app.sval.updater, with the connection
app.sval.updater.server; the disk image installer's is
app.sval.dmgInstallHelper; updater.app and crashreporter.app take app.sval.
identifiers.

The requirements Sval's app and its updater helper check each other's code
signature against (SMPrivilegedExecutables, SMAuthorizedClients) name the
team that signs Sval's releases, Ellm Tree's WN6TRJ4H8P; with Mozilla's, the
elevated update refuses a Sval release's helper.

